Baker, Michael Burton, and Phil Joanou.

14
00:50:24,000 --> 00:50:30,000
It stars Joey Cramer as David Freeman, a 12-year-old boy abducted by an alien spaceship who,
as an unfortunate side-effect, is transported eight years into the future.

15
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
It features an early film appearance by Sarah Jessica Parker as Carolyn
McAdams, a key character in the future whom David befriends.

16
00:57:36,000 --> 00:57:42,000
The film's producers initially sent the project to Walt Disney Pictures in 1984, but the studio was unable to approve it, and it
was sent to Producers Sales Organization, which made a deal with Disney to distribute it in the United States.

17
01:01:12,000 --> 01:01:18,000
It was partially shot in Fort Lauderdale, Florida, and Norway, being
a co-production with Norwegian company Viking Film.

18
01:04:48,000 --> 01:04:54,000
The film is notable for being one of the first Hollywood films to use
extensive computer-generated imagery (CGI) effects.

19
01:08:24,000 --> 01:08:30,000
Specifically, it was the first use of image-based lighting and
an early use of morphing in a motion picture.

20
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
It is also known to be one of the first Hollywood productions to feature an entirely electronic music film
score, composed using a Synclavier, one of the first digital multitrack recorders and samplers.

21
01:15:36,000 --> 01:15:42,000
The film has since developed a cult following among
science-fiction and Disney fans.

22
